NIR spectrometer (Perkin Elmer Lambda 950). LogP is defined as the logarithm of the ratio of the concentrations of the complex in the organic and aqueous phases: logP = log([Concentration]octanol / [Concentration]PBS) or equivalently logP = log((OD)octanol / (OD)PBS)"}]}